  "notes": "Ordinary inference timings remain wall clock. Stage diagnostics deliberately fence upload, compute, and readback; their medians are not additive and do not reconstruct ordinary inference latency. Upload completion and readback map waits include browser scheduling/IPC and are not pure bus transfer time. Compute GPU timestamps exclude upload/readback/query resolve; compute host completion includes query resolve/copy when enabled. Single-dispatch timestamps can be quantized to zero; repeated timestamps amortize 100 dispatches, changing the workload. Resident runs reuse the last uploaded batch, exclude encoding/upload/readback, and amortize completion over 200 dispatches. CPU calls include WASM boundary copies. Timer precision and browser load affect results.",
